{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477147-cabal-types-member-proximity-public-association-role-in-chantry-mage-society","id":1477147,"title":"Cabal Types: member-proximity, public association, role in Chantry/Mage Society","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-23T19:12:38-07:00","id":1477147,"title":"Cabal Types: member-proximity, public association, role in Chantry/Mage Society","content":"I will just start with two completely different types of Cabals.<br /> <br /> The first kind is the one players usually play. The Mages live together, go most places together and cast beneficial magic on each other. <br /> <br /> The second more closely fits the definition of a Cabal. Members hide their association with each other and carry out a clandestine agenda in the community. They would make use of a Mindlink to coordinate their activities.<br /> <br /> Cabals can be specialized in different roles, which include:<br /> <br /> Espionage<br /> Entrepreneurship<br /> Exploring the Umbra<br /> Enchanting<br /> Acolyte Mentorship<br /> Pioneering (find a city with no other Mages and take over) <br /> <br /> What other roles would you add?<br /> <br /> As a storyteller, thinking of NPCs, how closely do members associate in public view? What roles do you assign NPC Cabals, if any?<br /> <br /> As a player, what would you want your Cabal doing most often?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T10:00:57-07:00","id":1477341,"title":"","content":"To your point about associating with one another in secret, and considering the ease with which cabals can be formed (i.e., it's not like a werewolf pack,) I tend to think that a mage could be in various cabals simultaneously, with similarly varying degrees of visibility. They might be in one cabal that has to do with putting money into public works projects that (they believe) will promote values in a community conducive to a particular sort of reality zone; they could be members of a cabal dedicated to a certain sort of research that that only meets virtually once per month; they could be in a cabal centered around sharing a small node or chantry that serves as their home base (like their <i>main</i> cabal); they could be members of a cabal that functions like a capital investment fund; and they could, at any given moment, but asked to join (or perhaps even conscripted,) into a cabal that operates like a task force, complete with a charter outlining a very narrow and specific purpose (e.g, <i>find and destroy the source of the Nephandic corruption that's trying to get a local park re-zoned for industrial waste disposal</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T16:03:38-07:00","id":1477370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477147-cabal-types-member-proximity-public-association-role-in-chantry-mage-society?p=1477341#post1477341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To your point about associating with one another in secret, and considering the ease with which cabals can be formed (i.e., it's not like a werewolf pack,) I tend to think that a mage could be in various cabals simultaneously, with similarly varying degrees of visibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Overlapping Cabal memberships was something I considered long ago. A troupe of players are usually not going to have any character who is a member of another cabal. The storyteller would have to assume the role of all the NPCs in the other cabal and play out that dialogue with the one player while the rest of the troupe check their text messages. When sketching out NPCs, the storyteller isn't limited by such constraints. A Chantry can be a network of overlapping cabals with certain members functioning as specialized envoys. When coming up with Mentor NPCs, I think of them as having been part of a cabal that still technically exists, but rarely meets, the experienced Mages having pursued a more individual path.<br /> <br /> The question that comes to mind is: To what degree does membership in a particular cabal constitute a group identity? Most cabals, I would think, are going to have one member with Mind 3 who is capable of facilitating a Mind-link between everyone. Frequent use of such close communication has a potential to immerse the individual into said group identity. In the Traditions, differences between paradigms are something for which that kind of fusion could be considered a remedy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477147-cabal-types-member-proximity-public-association-role-in-chantry-mage-society?p=1477341#post1477341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might be in one cabal that has to do with putting money into public works projects that (they believe) will promote values in a community conducive to a particular sort of reality zone; they could be members of a cabal dedicated to a certain sort of research that that only meets virtually once per month; they could be in a cabal centered around sharing a small node or chantry that serves as their home base (like their <i>main</i> cabal); they could be members of a cabal that functions like a capital investment fund; and they could, at any given moment, but asked to join (or perhaps even conscripted,) into a cabal that operates like a task force, complete with a charter outlining a very narrow and specific purpose (e.g, <i>find and destroy the source of the Nephandic corruption that's trying to get a local park re-zoned for industrial waste disposal</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Most who succeed in these objectives would have the opportunity to build on their success. I also think that three of the four Essences are conducive to different kinds of approaches. Individual members (or their Avatars) would bring that flavor into the project. <br /> Pattern: Small, achievable goals, each built on the success of the last.<br /> Questing: Pursuing the ideal, no matter the odds, for as long as it takes.<br /> Dynamic: Being the force of change that breaks down barriers and resistance.<br /> <br /> In the case of the anti-Nephandi task force, it's more likely that it would dissolve, having fulfilled its specific mandate. You could have one member (nature: cavalier) who wishes to be reunited with those they fought alongside, trying to uncover more Wyrm-Blights to report, others (some of who were conscripts) thankful for having survived and laying low to avoid being dragged to the abyss by more powerful adversaries. <br /> <br /> Two strategies my troupe is currently considering:<br /> 1) Stealing Technocracy equipment, weapons and wonders. <br /> 2) Poaching their Extraordinary Citizens (ECs). ECs can't be told everything. Some might not even know very much about who they work for, due to the need for deniability. Exploiting loose connections is something we're giving thought to right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}